==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc}} {{term|κένωσις||emptying|sc=polytonic}}, from {{term|κενόειν||to empty|sc=polytonic}} (with reference to Philippians 2.vii, "But he emptied himself, taking the form of a slave, becoming as human beings are" – New Jerusalem Version).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/kɪˈnəʊsɪs/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|kenos|es|-}}

# {{Christianity}} [[Christ]]'s voluntary [[divestment]] of his divine powers.

